    "tree_id": "b823e358cafcf01c45f89b98ab99421846b1efe5",
    "message": "chore: adopt qualified branch, planning and continuation fixes (#564)\n\nInstalled workers and CI callbacks still execute older harness\nrevisions. Pin every installed worker and both callbacks to qualified\nsource `ea5ce4fd1e09bb98e2c520d132a826c24cb50e0a` (CLI 0.12.60 / SDLC\n0.21.11), bringing canonical publication branches, host-owned planning\nmetadata and bounded continuation recovery into the source repository's\ninstalled behavior.\n\nQualification: [#547\noriginals](https://github.com/juangcarmona/lighthouse/tree/252f18fc64b3cd8bde0be477b55416eaead4b8b1/acceptance/20261107-followups/547),\n[#414\noriginals](https://github.com/juangcarmona/lighthouse/tree/208a09151979604f86fda82532ab1a4d1c874ddb/acceptance/20261107-followups/414),\nand [#541 native\nproof](https://github.com/juangcarmona/lighthouse/tree/66fe79305ae64e9afe82596cd229ac39c98bb9fd/acceptance/20261107-followups/541).\nThe last case confirms a rejected worker with skipped effects and one\naccepted linked review, reusing its merge, CI and product apply. Its\nmaintenance wake-up was explicitly invoked after a missing scheduled\nevent; #567 tracks automatic wake-up latency. The controlled\nfault-carrier correction and supervised seed are retained.\n\nOnly workflow projections change. Models, execution policies and\ncompletion subscription membership are preserved, including the\nconcurrent runtime change `860624f`. Package CI now validates a pending\nChangesets release plan when one exists. Repository verification,\npackage contracts, a clean consumer and workflow validation pass. No\nacceptance hooks are installed in Lighthouse.",
    "timestamp": "2026-11-08T01:28:56Z",
